  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0488, and it contains four tables: Department, Employee_Table, Email_Configuration, and Employee_Maintenance_Email_Server.\nThe Department table has the following columns: Allow_Customer_Work_Orders, Department_ID (primary key), Description, Disable_Auto_Reply, Email, Hide_Department, Name, Reply_by_Email_Only, Request_Feedback, and Sorting_Order. The Department_ID column is a primary key, and the other columns are of type VARCHAR(255).\nThe Employee_Table table has the following columns: Department_ID, Employee_ID (primary key), Gender, Name, and Phone. The Employee_ID column is a primary key, and the other columns are of type VARCHAR(255).\nThe Email_Configuration table has the following columns: Configuration_ID (primary key), Department_ID (foreign key), Host_Address, Login_Password, Login_Username, Port_Number. The Configuration_ID column is a primary key, and the other columns are of type VARCHAR(255).\nThe Employee_Maintenance_Email_Server table has the following columns: Employee_ID (foreign key), Maintenance_Time, Server_ID (foreign key), and PRIMARY KEY (Employee_ID, Server_ID, Maintenance_Time). The Employee_ID and Server_ID columns are foreign keys that reference the Employee_ID and Configuration_ID columns in the Employee_Table and Email_Configuration tables, respectively.\nIn summary, this schema contains four tables that represent a company's departments, employees, email configurations, and employee maintenance email servers. The tables are related through foreign keys, and the primary keys and unique constraints ensure data integrity.",
  "gold_question": "This backend system is designed for managing work order processing information across different support departments.\n1.Department Management:The system allows you to create, modify, and delete different support departments. For each department, you can set:\nDepartment name, description, and email address.Sorting order. Whether the department only allows customers to submit work orders.Whether work orders are only responded to via email pipeline.Whether auto-replies are disabled.Whether the department is hidden from users.\n2.Email Configuration:For each department, configure the email server’s host address, port number, login username, and password, allowing the system to automatically handle emails.\n3.Employee Email Server Maintenance:\nEmployees can maintain the email server in real-time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0488.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0488\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `allow_customer_work_orders` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `disable_auto_reply` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hide_department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reply_by_email_only` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_feedback` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sorting_order` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_table` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `email_configuration` (\n  `configuration_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `host_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `port_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`configuration_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `email_configuration_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_maintenance_email_server` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `server_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `server_id`, `maintenance_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_maintenance_email_server_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee_table` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_maintenance_email_server_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`server_id`) REFERENCES `email_configuration` (`configuration_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
